whileOpT -- SEQ 580 (Tony, 2026-11-09): WHILe as an operator. WHILe declares op= and its hand action is deleted; a default
action builds its instruct from its label. whileT (both roads) must not move; these rows pin what the default CHANGES and two
controls it must not. Rows prefixed WO-. Interpreted only.

WO-1  the body slot refuses: today "REFUSED WHILe -- its statement handed up no instruct" (WHILe's own refusal, pinned by no
      row until now); the default names the slot by its label and, the body having handed up nothing, says so.
WO-2  the condition slot refuses: today F-147's attach refusal naming the internal list (whileArms, F-148); the default names
      the slot by its label.
WO-3  control: a bare-name condition is a value, not an instruct, and is not refused (the default demands an instruct only
      from a STATEMENt slot).
WO-4  control: the old road's WhilE, a refused body in an action: refused naming xl1, the rest of the action does not run.

Not run alone: pop.sh appends the row, print "NEXT", a sentinel; one process per row. Each row reads exit and sentinel; stdout
(lines joined by |); and the REFUSED lines that name WHILe, whileArms or xl1, joined by |.

SEQ 596 R1 (Tony, 2026-11-10): one refusal per statement. The refusals column now holds EVERY REFUSED line of the run (and
any parse failed line), so it reads how many there are: today the first refusal and then the default action's line for the slot
that handed up nothing; intended the first refusal alone.

